===Etymology===
* (''Venray'') First attested as ''de Heijde'' in 1838-1857. Derived from {{m|nl|heide|t=heath, heathland}}.
* (''Friesland'') First attested as ''De Heyde'' in 1718. {{clq|nl|fy|De Heide}}, derived from {{m|fy|heide|t=heath, heathland}}.
* (''Heumen'') Derived from {{m|nl|heide|t=heath, heathland}}.
* (''Montferland'') First attested as ''Diemsche Heyde'' in 1729. Derived from {{m|nl|heide|t=heath, heathland}}.
* (''Echt-Susteren'') First attested as ''Heijde'' in 1838-1857. Derived from {{m|nl|heide|t=heath, heathland}}.
* (''Leudal, Heythuysen'') First attested as ''Heide'' in 1899. Derived from {{m|nl|heide|t=heath, heathland}}. See also {{cog|li|Hei}}, {{m|li|De Heihoezer}}.
* (''Leudal, Roggel'') First attested as ''Heide'' in 1835. Derived from {{m|nl|heide|t=heath, heathland}}.
* (''Roermond'') First attested as ''Heijer huysen'' in the second half of the 17th century. Derived from {{m|nl|heide|t=heath, heathland}}. See also {{cog|li|De Hei}}.

